From: ARM64 enablement — add ARM64 codegen flags to gcc.cmake

Adds an elseif() branch for ARM64 alongside the existing i386/amd64
arch-specific compile options. These flags are required for stable
ARM64 codegen under both GCC and Clang (gcc.cmake handles both):

  -fno-optimize-sibling-calls : prevents tail-call optimization that
      can confuse stack unwinding through the ARM64 exception model.
  -fno-omit-frame-pointer     : required by _AddressOfReturnAddress()
      and by reliable kernel stack walking.
  -mstrict-align              : ARM64 default ABI permits unaligned
      access, but kernel and HAL code uses MMIO regions where
      unaligned access traps. Force strict alignment to match the
      Windows ARM64 kernel build options.

No other arches affected — purely additive.

---
 sdk/cmake/gcc.cmake | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sdk/cmake/gcc.cmake b/sdk/cmake/gcc.cmake
--- a/sdk/cmake/gcc.cmake
+++ b/sdk/cmake/gcc.cmake
@@ -254,6 +254,8 @@
         add_compile_options(-mpreferred-stack-boundary=4)
     endif()
+elseif(ARCH STREQUAL "arm64")
+    add_compile_options(-fno-optimize-sibling-calls -fno-omit-frame-pointer -mstrict-align)
 endif()

 # Other
